{{> Top frame}}
<header>
  <p class="kicker">Go deeper</p>
  <h1>Database</h1>
  <p class="lede">SQLite inside the server, and SQL that is typed: roux-db reads your queries
  and writes Roc functions for them.</p>
</header>

<section class="book">
  <form method="post" action="/guestbook">
    <input name="name" placeholder="Your name" maxlength="40" required>
    <input name="message" placeholder="Say something" maxlength="280" required>
    <button>Sign</button>
  </form>
  <ul class="signatures">
{{#signatures}}    <li><b>{{ name }}</b> <span>{{ message }}</span> <time>{{ signed_at }}</time></li>
{{/signatures}}  </ul>
{{^signatures}}  <p class="empty">No one has signed yet. Be first.</p>
{{/signatures}}</section>

<section class="turn-box">
  <h2>Your turn</h2>
  <p>Sign the book. Then show how many have signed, through all three layers:</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><p>A query, in <code>db/Guestbook.sql</code>:</p>
    <pre><code>-- name: count :one
-- @column total : I64
SELECT count(*) AS total FROM signature;</code></pre>
    <p>roux-db checks it against <code>db/schema.sql</code> and writes
    <code>Guestbook.count!</code> into <code>db/Guestbook.roc</code>.</p></li>
    <li><p>In <code>templates/Book.rocstache</code>, under the form:
    <code>&lt;p&gt;&#123;&#123; total &#125;&#125; signed&lt;/p&gt;</code>. Save: roc now says
    <code>Book.template</code> needs a <code>Book.Ctx</code>, which has a <code>total</code>
    (<code>templates/Book.roc</code> shows it) that <code>main.roc</code> does not give yet.</p></li>
    <li><p>In <code>main.roc</code>, in <code>book!</code>, read the count and pass it on:</p>
    <pre><code>signatures = Guestbook.recent!(Sqlite.read(db, request))?
{ total } = Guestbook.count!(Sqlite.read(db, request))?
Ok(Rocstache.html(Book.template({
	frame: frame("/guestbook"),
	nav: nav("/guestbook"),
	signatures,
	total: total.to_str(),
})))</code></pre>
    <p>The template's fields are strings unless it declares a contract, so the count is made
    one here.</p></li>
  </ol>
  <p>Get one layer wrong and its tool says so: roux-db for the SQL, roc for the Roc, roux for
  the template.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Where it lives</h2>
  <p><code>tutor.db</code>, beside <code>main.roc</code>, made from <code>db/schema.sql</code>
  the first time the app starts. Reads run on every thread at once; a write takes the one
  writer (<code>Sqlite.write!</code>) and ends with <code>Sqlite.commit!</code>.</p>
  <p>Editing a query is like editing Roc: roux-db rewrites its module, roc builds, the app
  restarts, and a query roux-db refuses shows over the page with its line. Changing
  <code>db/schema.sql</code> changes the database too, as the app restarts: add a column with a
  <code>DEFAULT</code> and every signature keeps its row, with that value. A table or column that goes is refused until a step in
  <code>db/ledger.sql</code> renames or drops it, and the refusal, in this tab, writes the
  step for you. How it works:
  <a href="https://github.com/Eldhus/roux/blob/master/docs/migrations.md">roux's migrations</a>.</p>
</section>
{{> Bottom nav}}
